Linux - Godot-v3.6.1-stable - glsl2\n\n### Issue description\n\ndepending of the text, it doesnt break line correctly\nin the image, if I type tttt it breaks line but the text ended inside of him.\n\n<img width=\"446\" height=\"279\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3f55aa4-5111-4414-bbe3-21c391319d0f\" />\n\nI made some test here. The first thing is that  it also happens on editor:\n\n<img width=\"726\" height=\"161\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ff5d9605-40de-423d-ae3a-0175cb052b59\" />\n\nthe next thing was to check if it was the tag. And yeah, it happens only with tag in the text.\n\n<img width=\"944\" height=\"247\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc7d67e4-fbcd-43ae-9548-f6153336c3d5\" />\n\nnow testing if it happens even with other font. And like I propose, it depends of the font \n\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"133\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65780332-c9e5-453e-9aba-b2d5d75ebfab\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nfirst you need the font, the one that I using is from this pack https://somepx.itch.io/humble-fonts-free\nI using the compass-pro one\n\nthe configuration of the font is:\n- Size: 32\n- outline size: 1\n- extra_spacing/top: -4\n- extra_spacing/bottom: -2\n- extra_spacing/char: 4\n\nthe richtextlabel size that I using is Vector2(408, 264) and it have bbcode active.\nput this text on it:[color=yellow]{11111111111111111}:[/color] tttt\ncuriosity, it dont happens if the text is like this: [color=yellow]{11111111111111111}: [/color]tttt\nit also happens with others tags like wave\n\nI really hope that this helps to give a direction to where is the problem, that I think it is from the way the richlabel treats tags in the text.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nit only happens on godot 3\n\n[example.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21392233/example.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"no